===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|military}} A large [[artillery]] gun or one of the largest-caliber [[naval]] guns (as on a [[battleship]]).
#* '''1870''' Dec. 2, "[http://paperspast.natlib.govt.nz/cgi-bin/paperspast?a=d&d=ST18701202.2.11 The Suez Mail]," ''Southland Times'' (New Zealand), Issue 1342, p. 2:
#*: London, Nov. 1: The '''big guns''' opened fire on Paris today at mid-day.
#* '''1968''' March 26, "[http://news.google.com/newspapers?id=tSFgAAAAIBAJ&sjid=ZG4NAAAAIBAJ&pg=3437,4076814&dq=her-big-guns+battleship&hl=en Battleship begins Viet Tests]," ''Evening News'' (Newburgh, NY, USA), p. 1 <small>(retrieved 19 Aug. 2011)</small>:
#*: The smaller crew was possible because the battleship was stripped of all but her '''big guns'''.
#* '''2008''' Dec. 6, [[w:William J. Bennett|William J. Bennett]] and John Cribb, "[https://web.archive.org/web/20110812195412/http://www.dcourier.com/main.asp?SectionID=36 Deadly resolve answered attack ]," ''Daily Courier'' (USA) <small>(retrieved 19 Aug. 2011)</small>:
#*: The USS West Virginia became one of many symbols of American resolve. . . . Her '''big guns''' pounded the enemy at the battles of Leyte Gulf, Iwo Jima, and Okinawa.
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|by extension|usually [[pluralize]]d}} A person, group, thing, or course of action that is [[powerful]], [[influential]], or particularly [[effective]].
#* '''1888''' June 6, "[http://select.nytimes.com/gst/abstract.html?res=F30816F93C5E1A738DDDAE0894DE405B8884F0D3 A Great Day for Big Guns]," ''New York Times'' <small>(retrieved 20 Aug. 2011)</small>:
#*: This has been a great day for the big guns. This does not refer to Prof. Lummis and the other '''big guns''' of the Board of Visitors, for every day is a great one for them.
#* '''1957''' Aug. 28, Ed Wilks, "[http://news.google.com/newspapers?id=BgkeAAAAIBAJ&sjid=30UEAAAAIBAJ&pg=6689,5400266&dq=big-gun&hl=en Sports]" (Headline), ''Park City News'' (USA), p. 15 <small>(retrieved 20 Aug. 2011)</small>:
#*: Berra Is '''Big Gun''' In Yankee Victory
#* '''2001''' June 29, Frank Pellegrini, "[http://www.time.com/time/nation/article/0,8599,165668,00.html Whatever Happened to Military Restructuring?]," ''Time'':
#*: And the administration's '''big guns''' — Bush, Cheney, Powell and once-and-current Defense Secretary Donald Rumsfeld — had the clout to make bold and necessary changes.
#* '''2007''' March 26, Yuri Wuensch, "[http://jam.canoe.ca/Music/Artists/C/Clapton_Eric/ConcertReviews/2007/03/26/3835986.html Eric Clapton simply masterful]," ''canoe.ca'' (Canada) <small>(retrieved 20 Aug. 2011)</small>:
#*: Clapton kept the '''big guns''' for last, finishing the set off with Derek and the Domino's "Layla", complete with the haunting instrumentals at song's end.

